# Per-file merge strategies.
#
# `merge=union` keeps BOTH sides of every conflict block in the named
# file. It applies to `CHANGELOG.md`, whose conflicts are always false
# positives at the semantic level: every feature PR inserts a new bullet
# at the top of `## Unreleased`. Two PRs inserting at the same anchor
# produce a text-level conflict that git's default merge cannot resolve,
# even though the right answer is always "keep both entries". Union
# merge does exactly that.
#
# Drawback to know: union-merged conflicts are silently resolved by
# concatenation, so a deliberate rewrite (one branch rewords a bullet,
# the other deletes it) loses the deletion. Only appends and deletes
# merge reliably; rewrites need a manual pass at PR-author time.
CHANGELOG.md     merge=union
